# The composer format: one statement per line, indented lines are properties.
issue: Is Hermione warm-blooded, and does it follow that she has fur?
thesis: C3
party author: Author

predicate mammal (mammal): An animal of the class Mammalia.
predicate warm_blooded (warm-blooded): Maintains body temperature internally.
  aliases: endothermic
predicate has_fur (has fur)
entity hermione (Hermione): A particular cat.

C1 [certain, definition]: Every mammal is warm-blooded.
  logic: forall x: mammal(x) -> warm_blooded(x)
  terms: mammal, warm-blooded
C2 [certain, evidence]: Hermione is a mammal.
  logic: mammal(hermione)
  terms: Hermione, mammal
  source: Veterinary record | https://example.org/hermione
C3 [certain, derived]: Hermione is warm-blooded.
  logic: warm_blooded(hermione)
  terms: Hermione, warm-blooded
C5 [probable, derived]: Hermione has fur.
  logic: has_fur(hermione)
  terms: Hermione, has fur
C6 [probable]: Crookshanks is a mammal.
  terms: Crookshanks, mammal

A1 [deductive]: C1, C2 => C3
  title: Hermione is warm-blooded
  warrant: Universal instantiation of C1 at Hermione, then modus ponens with C2.
A2 [deductive]: C1, C2 => C5
  title: Hermione has fur
  warrant: Mammals are warm-blooded and Hermione is a mammal, so she has fur.
